<div id="2026-09-10-enrich-existing-supplier-and-sitename" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-09-10 — Enrich existing supplier; fix sitename mismatch; no orphan suppliers</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> When a supplier already exists, the AI now fills in its BLANK contact fields from the web before creating the invoice. Also fixed two defects found while debugging "No supplier found".</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why (enrichment).</strong> Previously the web lookup only ran on the <em>create</em> path — a matched supplier was used as-is, so rows with missing contact info (e.g. OpenRouter, Inc showing dashes) were never completed. Added <code>_enrich_existing_supplier</code>: it fills only empty or "-" fields and never overwrites existing values, so a scraped wrong value cannot clobber a good one.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why (sitename).</strong> <code>InvoiceCreate::sitename()</code> read <code>$c-&gt;stash-&gt;{SiteName}</code> FIRST, while <code>Controller::Inventory::_sitename()</code> reads <code>$c-&gt;session-&gt;{SiteName}</code> first. A chat request could therefore query a different sitename than the Inventory pages, find zero suppliers, report "No supplier found", and auto-create a duplicate. Resolution order now matches Inventory (session first).</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why (orphans).</strong> Supplier creation ran OUTSIDE the invoice transaction. When the invoice insert failed (e.g. the varchar(255) description abort), the supplier had already committed — leaving an orphan per retry. Both now share one <code>txn_do</code>, so a failed invoice rolls the supplier back.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Verified.</strong> Blank row → filled <code>email=support@openrouter.ai</code>, <code>website=https://openrouter.ai</code>. Populated row (TekSavvy) → only blank fields checked, existing email preserved, nothing overwritten. All syntax checks and prior regressions (parse/date, currency, receipt, match) still pass. Note: could not query the live DB to confirm row-level sitename values — every host in db_config.json was unreachable from the agent, so the sitename ordering defect is fixed as a code-level correctness issue.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>Comserv/lib/Comserv/Model/AI2/InvoiceCreate.pm</code>. The chat reply now reports which fields were filled so the user can verify.</p>
</div>
